      "textEn": "206\n\nPreviously, he himself, having joined, entered his own temple. Like a gem-studded mountain, the abode of the great king Mahendra. 28 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nPriyata - happy; Swayam - self; Taya - his; Yuktah - together; Pravishtah - going inside; Nija - own; Mandiram - in the house;\nMani - with jewels; Stambha - pillar; Shata - hundreds; Upetam - with; Maha-Indra - of the great king Indra of heaven; Bhavanam -\npalace; Yatha - like. He happily entered his house with his wife, where there were hundreds of\ngem-studded kha bhes, like in the palace of Devraj Mahendra. Commentary: Srila Vishwanath Chakravarthy explains that Sudama was surprised to see his wife. When he was in wonder as to who this divine wife is, who has come to a sinful man like me, then the maids\ninformed that she is his wife. At that moment, Sudama's body became young and beautiful, which\nwas adorned with excellent clothes and ornaments. The word 'previously' here indicates that he was extremely happy with these changes.\nIn the Mahabharata, in the Vishnu Sahasranama, the immortal description of Sudama's sudden opulence occurred in these words:\nShridama, the one who brought the glory of Indra to the earth for the sake of his humble devotee—Lord Vishnu, for the benefit of his humble devotee Shridama (Sudama), is also said to have brought the radiance of Indra to this earth. Payahphennibhaah shaya daanta rukmaparichhadaah. Parvanka hemdandani chaamaravyajanani cha. 29>. Asanani cha hamani mudupastarani cha. Muktadamvilambini vitanani dyumanti cha. 30>. In clean crystal wells, in great epidemics also. Adorned with jewels, shining like a river of jewels. 31st. Beyond the Brahmin, there is prosperity, all wealth.\nTarkayamas niravyaghrash swasamruddhimahaitukim. 32). Meaning of the word\n\nPayah - of milk; Phenah - of foam; Nibhah - similar; Shayah - bed, cot; Dantah - made of ivory; Rukma - golden;\nParichhadah - decoration; Paryankah - bed, Seats; gold - of gold; staff - of