      "textEn": "216\n\nEje cha bhagwan ramo yatrasprashtoopi karmana. 3. Lokasangrahayaniso yathanyoohapanuttaye. Great pilgrimages, there the Bharati people are. Vrishnayacha tatha krooravasudevahukaadayah. Yayurvatarasthatkhetram swamaghham kshapayishnavaah. 5. Gadapradyumnasambadhyah suchandrashukasaranaih. Aasteyaniruddho rakshayam kritavarma cha yuthapah. 6. Meaning of the word\n\nNikshitriyam—devoid of kings; Mahim—to the earth; Kurvan—by doing; Ramah—Parashurama; Shastra—weapons; Bhrutam—of those who hold; Varahah—the best; Nripam—of kings; Rudhir—of blood; Ogenah—by flood; Yatra—where; Chakre—\nmade; Maha—great; Hridan—lake, Lakes; EJ—worshiped; Ch—and; Bhagavan—God; Ramah—Parashurama; Yatra—where; Asparsha—untouched; Api—even though; Karmana—by action and its fruits; Lokam—the world; Sangrahayan—to receive; Upadhyayan—to preach; Isha—God; Yatha—as; Anyah—another person; Agha—sin; Apanuttaya—to remove; Mahatyam—great;\nOn the occasion of the holy pilgrimage; there—there; Agam—coming; Bharati—of Bharatvarsha; Praja—people;\nVrishnayah—members of the Vrishni caste; Cha—and; Tatha—also; Akrur-Vasudev-ahuk-ayah—Akrur, Vasudev, Ahuk (Ugrasena)\nand others; Yayuh—went; Bharat—this Bharatvanshi (Parikshit); Tat—that; Kshetram—in the holy place; Swam—own; Agham—\nSins; Kshapayishnavah—willing to uproot; Gad-Pradyumna-Samb-ayah—Gad, Pradyumna, Samv etc.; Suchandra-Shuk-\nSaranaih—Suchandra, With Shuka and Sarana; Aaste—remains; Aniruddha—Aniruddha; Rakshayam—to protect; Kritavarma—\nKritavarma; Cha—and; Yuth-pah—army leader. After freeing the earth from kings, among the warriors, the supreme Lord Parashurama\ncreated vast lakes from the blood of kings in Samantapanchak. Although Parashurama\nwas not affected by the fruits of his actions, he still performed a Yagya there to educate the general public.\nIn this way, to free themselves from sins, they behaved like a common person. Now, in this Samantapanchak, for pilgrimage, from all parts of India, a very large number of people had come. Hey Bharatvanshi, among the people who came to this pilgrimage site,\nmany Vrajas, such as Gad, Pradyumna, and Samba—had come to get rid of their respective sins.\nThey had come. Akrur, Vasudev, Ahuk and other kings also went there. To protect Dwarka,\nwith Suchandra, Shuk, and Saran, along with Aniruddha and his armed forces,\nthe leader Kritavarma also remained. Meaning: According to Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti, to protect the city, Shri Krishna's grandson\nAniruddha remained in Dwarka because he is the original form of Lord Vishnu as the protector of the divine-world, the white island."
