      "textEn": "221\n\nKunti said—Queen Kunti said; Arya—Honorable; Bhrathah—Brother; Aham—I; Manye—I think; Atmanam—To oneself; Akruta—Failed to obtain; Ashisham—Desires; Yat—Because; Vai—Undoubtedly; Aapatsu—In times of trouble; Mat—To me; Vartam—What happened; Na Anusmaratha—You people do not remember; Sat-Tamah—Most virtuous in nature. Queen Kunti said: O my honorable brother, I feel that my wishes\nhave failed, because although all of you are of very gentle nature, but in the days of my calamities,\nyou have forgotten me. Note: Here, Maharani Kunti is addressing her brother Vasudeva. Friends, known, sons, brothers, and even fathers. Those who remember their own people as if it were a blessing from God. 19. Meaning of the word:\n\nFriend: - Friends; Known: - And relatives; Sons: - Sons; Brothers: - Brothers; Parents: - Parents; Also - also; They do not remember -\nThey do not remember; Dear ones - dear ones; Whose - Whose; Fate - Creator; Unexpected - Unfavorable.\nOn whom the creator does not remain favorable, his friends and family members, even children,\nbrothers and parents also forget their loved ones. Meaning: Srila Sridhar Swami and Vishwanath Chakravarti Thakur both have commented that Kunti\ndoes not blame her relatives for her suffering. She calls them extremely gentle-natured.\nShe says. They curse their misfortune for the cause of their sorrow. Srivasudeva said,\nAmba, the one who is smeared with mud, is the one who is pleasing to God. The people are controlled by the Lord, and they perform their duties. 20>. Meaning of the word.\n\nShri-Vasudeva said—Shri Vasudeva said; Amb—Hey sister; Ma—mother; Asman—From us; Asuyeathah—Be angry; Daiv—By fate; Kridanakan—Toys; Naran—To humans; Ishasya—Of God; Hi—Undoubtedly; Vashe—Subject; Lokah—Individual; Kurute—Is done by oneself; Karyate—Is done by others; Atha Va—Or else. Shri Vasudev said: Oh sister, do not be angry with us. We are the toys of fate for ordinary people.\nUndoubtedly, whether a man acts on h