      "textEn": "222\n\nThus, again, the place is destroyed by the divine. 21. Meaning of the word\n\nKansa—by Kansa; Pratapitah—very much tormented; Sarve—all; Vayam—we; Yatah—having gone; Disham—in different directions; Etarhi eva—just now; Punah—again; Sthanam—to their respective places; Daiven—by the creator; Asaditah—\nBrought; Swasah—O sister. Hey sister, we, oppressed by Kansa, had fled in various directions, but by the grace of the creator,\nEventually, we have been able to return to our respective homes. Srisuka said:\nVasudeva, the first of the gods, and others, were worshipped by the kings. Those who are always absorbed in the supreme bliss of the unbroken vision. 22. Meaning of the word\n\nShri-Shuka said—Shri Shukadeva Goswami said; Vasudeva-Ugrasena-Aadyaha—Vasudeva, Ugrasena, etc.; Yadubhiha—by the Yadavas;\nTe—they; Architaha—respected; Nripaaha—Kings; Asan—became; Achyuta—of Lord Krishna; Sandarsha—from the sight; Param—Supreme; Aananda—in bliss; Nirvritaaha—Peaceful.\n.\n\nShukdev Goswami said: Vasudev, Ugrasen, and other Yadus honored those various kings\nwho, upon seeing Lord Achyuta, became extremely delighted, overwhelmed with joy, and satisfied. Bhishma, Drona, Ambika's son, Gandhari's son, and so on. Sadaraha Pandavah, Kunti, Sanjayo, Vidurah, Kripa. 23). Kuntibhoja, Viratascha, Bhishmaka, Nagnajinmahat. Purujidrupadaha, Shalyo Dhrishtaketuha, Sa Kashirat. 2. Dumghosho Vishalaksho Maithilo Madrakayau. Yudhamanyu, Susharma, and his wife Bahvikayadhayah. 25. Oh kings, these kings, O Yudhishthira, are devoted to me.\nBeautiful women with grace, seeing them, they are mesmerized. 26. Meaning of the words:\n\nBhishma, Drona, Ambika's son—Bhishma, Drona, and the son of Ambika (Dhritarashtra); Gandhari—Gandhari; Sa—with; Suta—his\nson; Tatha—also; Sa-darah—with wives; Pandava—Pandu's son; Kunti—Kunti; Sanjaya—Vidura; Kripa—Kripa; Kuntibhoja—Vrata and\nKripa; Kuntibhoja—Vrata and Virata; Bhishmaka—Bhishmaka; Nagnajit—Nagnajit; Mahan—Great; Purujit—Pur